     "name": "Chris Chelios",
     "description": "1995 Western Conference Quarterfinals Netcam-Breaking Goal: On May 11, 1995, in the Western Conference Quarterfinals against Toronto at Maple Leaf Gardens, Chelios scored a shorthanded goal that broke the NHL netcam. In the third period of Game 3, with the Blackhawks up 2-1, No. 7 went blue line to blue line and fired a powerful slapshot past F\u00e9lix Potvin\u2019s glove and through the NHL\u2019s camera. Chicago would go on to win the game 3-2 and the series in seven games, advancing to the Western Conference Semifinals.\n\nOfficially Licensed Product of the NHL, NHLPA, and/or NHLAA. All copyright, logos, and marks are the property of their respective owners and are used, under license, by Sweet. All Rights Reserved. [Terms Apply](https://nhlbreakaway.com/terms).",
